data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(trimmed: the same JSON as structuredContent)"}],"structuredContent":{"description":"<p><br>Title: Wireless Software Engineer<br>Location: Austin, TX<br>Duration:12 Months Contract</p><p><br>What You'll Do<br>Design, develop, and enhance software features within wireless communication systems and protocol stacks.<br>&bull; Develop production-quality software in C/C++ and Python for Linux-based environments.<br>&bull; Analyze and debug complex issues across Layer 1 (PHY), Layer 2 (MAC/RLC/PDCP), and Layer 3 (RRC/NAS) protocols.<br>&bull; Investigate and troubleshoot issues across the full protocol stack, including areas outside your primary domain expertise, collaborating with development teams to drive root-cause resolution.<br>&bull; Diagnose and resolve complex issues encountered during customer deployments, integrations, and performance optimization activities.<br>&bull; Modify existing software and develop new code to address customer-specific requirements and technical challenges.<br>&bull; Develop APIs, software tools, automation frameworks, and diagnostics that improve development productivity and system visibility.<br>&bull; Analyze signaling logs, traces, packet captures, performance metrics, and timing behavior to identify root causes of system issues.<br>&bull; Build prototypes and rapidly validate new features and protocol enhancements.<br>&bull; Enhance existing Keysight software through feature development, performance improvements, and customer-driven innovations.<br>&bull; Participate in code reviews and contribute to software quality, maintainability, and engineering best practices.<br>&bull; Develop a deep understanding of Keysight software architecture, feature implementation, and protocol stack behavior to e ectively diagnose and resolve complex technical issues.<br>&bull; Collaborate closely with Keysight R&D teams to translate field findings into product improvements, software enhancements, and new capabilities.<br>&bull; Lead technical discussions with customers and provide guidance on protocol implementation, system architecture, and performance optimization.<br>&bull; Contribute to software releases, validation activities, and deployment of new features into customer development environments.</p><p><br>Required Qualifications<br>&bull; Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field.<br>&bull; 6+ years of experience in software development for wireless communication systems.<br>&bull; Strong software development experience in C/C++ and Python.<br>&bull; Experience developing software in Linux environments.<br>&bull; Solid understanding of 4G LTE, 5G NR, or 5G-Advanced technologies.<br>&bull; Deep understanding of 3GPP protocols across Layers 1-3, particularly RRC and NAS.<br>&bull; Hands-on software development experience within one or more wireless protocol stack layers, including PHY, MAC, RLC, PDCP, RRC, or NAS.<br>&bull; Proven experience as an R&D, platform, systems, or protocol-stack development engineer with demonstrated ownership of software design, implementation, debugging, and maintenance.<br>&bull; Experience investigating and troubleshooting complex software and protocol issues across multiple layers of the wireless stack.<br>&bull; Strong root-cause analysis and debugging skills using logs, traces, packet captures, signaling analysis, performance metrics, and software debugging tools.<br>&bull; Familiarity with 3GPP specifications and wireless protocol implementation.<br>&bull; Strong understanding of software architecture and development processes, with the ability to understand, modify, and extend existing codebases.</p><p><br>&bull; Experience participating in code reviews and working within collaborative software development environments.<br>&bull; Ability to design, develop, test, and deliver production-quality software.<br>&bull; Strong problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills. Ideal Candidate The ideal candidate combines deep wireless protocol expertise with strong hands-on software development skills and a demonstrated ability to design, implement, debug, and enhance production software systems. They enjoy solving di icult technical problems, working directly with cutting-edge customers, and collaborating with R&D teams to deliver innovative solutions. This role is best suited for engineers with strong software development and protocol-stack implementation experience who enjoy combining product development with customer-facing technical problem solving.</p>","skills":[{"name":"software development"},{"name":"wireless communication"},{"name":"C/C++"},{"name":"Python"},{"name":"4G LTE"},{"name":"5G NR"},{"name":"5G-Advanced technologies"},{"name":"PHY"},{"name":"Linux"}]},"isError":false}}

